[
  {
    "role": "paragraph",
    "segment": "Prescriptive models are prescriptions for the way software development should progress. Descriptive models describe the way software development is done in actuality. The model should reflect the goals of development, such as building high-quality software, finding faults early in development, and meeting required budget and schedule constraints. Creating a process model helps the development team find inconsistencies, redundancies, and omissions in the process and in its constituent parts.",
    "citations": [
      {
        "type": "source_text",
        "content": "Some are prescriptions for  the  way  software  development  should  progress, and  others  are descriptions of the way software development is done in actuality.",
