        "segment": "NSS (number of scenario scripts in the use cases) can be used as a size measure because it is correlated with application size and number of test cases, and it can feed an estimation model for predicting project effort or duration as well as help the test team prepare test cases and allocate resources for future testing activities.",
        "citations": [
            {
                "type": "source_text",
                "content": "Lorenz and Kidd count the number of scenario scripts (NSS) in the use cases. They report that this measure is correlated with application size and number of test cases.",
