[
    {
        "role": "paragraph",
        "segment": "Strategy for finding a reusable component: Establish a component inventory and use a feature-based evaluation to identify common, reusable pieces across past and planned projects. Create a matrix of features, rate each feature by whether it has been implemented and is still needed, and target features that are both needed and common to more than one project for reuse. Maintain regular reviews (weekly meetings) to inspect design documentation, monitor reuse levels, and drive redesigns to enhance reusability.",
        "citations": [
            {
                "type": "source_text",
                "content": "The Council created an inventory of components and formed a matrix with the features of all past  and  planned  projects. Then, each  feature  was  rated  in  terms  of  whether  it  had  been implemented and was still needed, had been implemented but was no longer needed, or had not been implemented but was still needed.Those features that were needed and were common to more than one project were targeted for reuse.",
                "img_id": null
            },
            {
                "type": "source_text",
                "content": "The Council  met  every  week  for  two  hours  to  make  component  selections, inspect design documentation for those components already in the repository, and to monitor the levels of reuse in the department's projects.",
                "img_id": null
            }
        ],
        "type": null
    },
    {
