[
  {
    "role": "paragraph",
    "segment": "Unit testing exercises each component separately, while integration testing puts components together in an organized way to help you isolate faults as the combined components are tested together. The objective of unit and integration testing was to ensure that the code implemented the design properly; that is, that the programmers wrote code to do what the designers intended.",
    "citations": [
      {
        "type": "source_text",
        "content": "Unit testing is the development activity that exercises each component separately; integration testing puts components together in an organized way to help you isolate faults as the combined components are tested together.",
        "img_id": null
      },
      {
        "type": "source_text",
        "content": "The objective of unit and integration testing was to ensure that the code implemented the design properly; that is, that the programmers wrote code to do what the designers intended.",
        "img_id": null
      }
    ],
    "type": null
  },
  {
    "role": "paragraph",
    "segment": "When to perform each: unit testing occurs as you develop individual components, and integration testing happens once we are satisfied that individual components are working correctly and meet our objectives, at which point we combine them into a working system.",
    "citations": [
      {
        "type": "source_text",
        "content": "When we are satisfied that individual components are working correctly and meet our objectives, we combine them into a working system.",
        "img_id": null
      },
      {
        "type": "source_text",
        "content": "The system is again viewed as a hierarchy of components, where each component belongs to a layer of the design.",
        "img_id": null
      }
    ],
    "type": null
  }
]

[
  {
    "role": "paragraph",
    "segment": "The gray polygon shows that Planning and requirements analysis and validation, test case generation, source code analysis, and coverage analysis require special treatment. Requirements are likely to be expressed in the requirements document, but there are few tools to support validation of requirements expressed as objects and methods. Likewise, most tools that assist in test case generation are not prepared to handle a model expressed in objects and methods. Most source code measurements are defined for procedural code, not for objects and methods. Over time, as researchers propose and test useful object-oriented measurements, this point of difference will diminish. Because it is the interaction of objects that is the source of complexity, code coverage measurements and tools are of less value in object-oriented testing than in traditional testing.",
    "citations": [
      {
        "type": "source_text",
        "content": "The gray polygon shows that Planning and requirements analysis and validation,test case generation,source code analysis,and coverage analysis require special treatment.",
        "img_id": null
      },
      {
        "type": "source_text",
        "content": "Requirements are likely to be expressed in the requirements document, but there are  few  tools  to  support  validation  of  requirements  expressed  as  objects  and methods.",
        "img_id": null
      },
      {
        "type": "source_text",
        "content": "Likewise, most tools that assist in test case generation are not prepared to handle a model expressed in objects and methods.",
        "img_id": null
      },
      {
        "type": "source_text",
        "content": "Most source code measurements are defined for procedural code, not for objects and  methods. Traditional  metrics  such  as  cyclomatic  numbers  are  of  little  use when assessing the size and complexity of object-oriented systems. Over time, as researchers propose and test useful object-oriented measurements, this point of difference will diminish.",
        "img_id": null
      },
      {
        "type": "source_text",
        "content": "Because it is the interaction of objects that is the source of complexity, code coverage measurements and tools are of less value in object-oriented testing than in traditional testing.",
        "img_id": null
      }
    ],
    "type": null
  }
]

