            }
        ],
        "type": null
    },
    {
        "role": "bullet",
        "segment": "Compare the types of faults found by inspections with those found later in testing or use (e.g., code inspections uncover code/low-level faults while testing may reveal requirements or architectural faults).",
        "citations": [
            {
                "type": "source_text",
                "content": "inspections identified mostly coding or low-level design faults, but testing discovered mostly requirements and architectural faults.",
                "img_id": null
            }
        ],
        "type": null
    },
    {
        "role": "bullet",
        "segment": "Ensure the evidence base covers preparation, familiarity with the product, and the environment of the inspections; a good year does not guarantee future success if conditions change.",
        "citations": [
            {
                "type": "source_text",
                "content": "the preparation rate, not the team size, determines inspection effectiveness.",
                "img_id": null
            },
            {
                "type": "source_text",
                "content": "the more familiarity, the better.",
                "img_id": null
            }
        ],
        "type": null
    },
    {
        "role": "paragraph",
        "segment": "Additionally, consider early involvement and design-focused reviews as a way to identify faults when they are easier and cheaper to fix, reducing the risk of late, costly fixes after delivery.",
        "citations": [
            {
                "type": "source_text",
                "content": "Moreover, the process benefits everyone by finding faults and problems when they are easy and inexpensive to correct.",
                "img_id": null
            },
            {
                "type": "source_text",
                "content": "The sooner we identify a problem, the fewer places in which we have to look to find its cause.",
                "img_id": null
            }
        ],
        "type": null
    }
]

[
